WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:02.949
(bright music)

00:00:05.151 --> 00:00:08.893
- McDonald's is truly an icon
of the 20th and 21st century.

00:00:08.893 --> 00:00:12.086
- Today we are trying
bloody Aussie Macca's,

00:00:12.086 --> 00:00:15.003
that you can only get in Australia.

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.646
- I don't know, I'm a little bit nervous.

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:21.229
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:24.778
- Oh my god.

00:00:24.778 --> 00:00:26.632
I mean it's the beetroot
that makes it really Aussie.

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:27.682
- It's the beetroot, yeah.

00:00:27.682 --> 00:00:28.515
- It's the bit of a...

00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:29.348
(snaps fingers)

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:30.331
sweetness that hits you.

00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:31.164
- If someone gave me this burger,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.239
I wouldn't assume it was from McDonald's,

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:33.815
I would assume it's from the corner shop.

00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:36.375
- A fried egg with a good piece of bacon

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:37.675
on top of a bit of meat,

00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:39.646
like, that is, like,
couldn't get more Australian.

00:00:39.646 --> 00:00:41.452
- Australians love double meat.

00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:44.429
- It's almost now the Aussie burger but...

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:46.906
a little bit of sauce, 10 out of 10.

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:48.269
- I want Matty sauce.

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:50.333
- She's talking about ketchup.

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:51.541
- Yeah, ketchup.

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:54.042
(loud guitars)

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:55.250
- Ah, no...

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.541
- Molletes are a very
traditional Mexican breakfast.

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.640
- This is not a Mollete.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.169
- I am ready for disappointment.

00:01:01.169 --> 00:01:04.846
- I like it, and I don't
like regular Molletes so...

00:01:04.846 --> 00:01:07.792
- Seems like, if you were
stoned, in another country,

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:09.275
and you were trying to make Molletes,

00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:10.747
you would make this.

00:01:10.747 --> 00:01:13.420
- Molletes are made with this
traditional Mexican bread,

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.618
called bollilo, like a really,
it's, like, sort of hard

00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:19.965
on the outside, soft on the inside bread.

00:01:19.965 --> 00:01:23.933
And it's like - you couldn't
do this with bollilo bread.

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:26.516
(upbeat music)

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.700
(upbeat guitars)

00:01:58.088 --> 00:01:59.457
- I don't think it needs the extra bun.

00:01:59.457 --> 00:02:00.804
- Yeah, me either.

00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:03.589
- Can anyone really describe
what McDonald's tastes like?

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.047
- The cheese and the
vegetables, ratio is great.

00:02:06.047 --> 00:02:09.034
But then you have this
interesting middle bun

00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:10.637
that kind of screws everything up.

00:02:10.637 --> 00:02:12.702
- But the funny thing is you
could take this top half off

00:02:12.702 --> 00:02:13.535
and just eat it like a burger.

00:02:13.535 --> 00:02:14.520
(laughs)

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.898
- My notes would be: the
middle bun, unnecessary,

00:02:16.898 --> 00:02:17.949
but I liked it.

00:02:17.949 --> 00:02:20.532
(upbeat music)

00:02:21.988 --> 00:02:22.880
- Oh, okay.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.965
- This looks interesting.

00:02:23.965 --> 00:02:24.798
- Interesting.

00:02:24.798 --> 00:02:28.755
- It's got all this,
all these little marks.

00:02:28.755 --> 00:02:30.588
(Mmm)

00:02:31.763 --> 00:02:33.185
- A little bit dry?

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:34.018
(laughs)

00:02:34.018 --> 00:02:35.336
- You look like you're
about to choke on it.

00:02:35.336 --> 00:02:37.450
The sauce on the bottom, I
don't like when they do that,

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.811
I always like my sauce on the top.

00:02:38.811 --> 00:02:41.721
The chicken's quite nice,
there's a little bit of a kick.

00:02:41.721 --> 00:02:42.554
- Still gonna eat it.

00:02:42.554 --> 00:02:43.730
- But it's still a cheap burger.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.489
- I actually got a bit of smokiness there.

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:47.469
I like chicken, I think it's okay.

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:48.891
I think I would order this again.

00:02:48.891 --> 00:02:51.474
(exotic music)

00:03:15.724 --> 00:03:17.603
(upbeat guitars)

00:03:17.603 --> 00:03:20.142
- I feel like McDonald's
is like Britney Spears,

00:03:20.142 --> 00:03:22.119
even if you deny that you don't like her,

00:03:22.119 --> 00:03:23.206
you do like her.

00:03:23.206 --> 00:03:26.649
- McDonald's is great,
Mexican food is great,

00:03:26.649 --> 00:03:29.311
the both of them combined, not that much.

00:03:29.311 --> 00:03:30.283
- You've done well McDonald's,

00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:33.616
you're replicating good Australian life.

00:03:35.638 --> 00:03:38.248
(upbeat guitars)

00:03:38.248 --> 00:03:40.632
(squeaky sound effects)

